Write a function `top_k_strings/2` that takes a list of strings and a non-negative integer `k`, and returns a list of at most `k` strings. The strings should be ordered by descending length (longest first). When strings have equal length, they should retain the order from the input list (i.e., stable sort by length descending). The function should return an empty list if `k` is zero or the input list is empty. If `k` exceeds the number of strings, return all strings sorted as described. The function should have a time complexity of O(n log n) where n is the number of strings in the input list.
